 "text": "Even the moon has wrinkles, and the research team counted more than 8,900 of them. The moon looks smooth in the night sky, but up close it seems to have quite a lot of wrinkles. But there's no need for beauty serum. These wrinkles offer clues to how the moon shrank and to its surprising way of dressing. The team used camera images from the lunar probe Elaro. They searched for cliffs on the moon's surface and marked them on a map. A wrinkle is a cliff with one steep side and one gentler side. These cliffs are thought to show where solid rock was squeezed together, with one side pushed up over the other. They are a record of a huge shoving match carved into the moon's surface. Using this map to work out how much the moon has shrunk, the team estimated that its radius had become about 42 to 46 meters smaller. By reading the wrinkles on its surface, scientists are investigating how a huge object in space has shrunk. Taking the Moon's measurements is quite a detailed job.",
